A16_SMSS_72_M016936_038                                                       
                                                                              
Apollo 16 Soil Mechanics                                                      
Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) Page C-5                             
                                                                              
These handwritten notes give the data from the postflight calibration         
tests of the Apollo 16 Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP)               
performed at the Lockheed Building in Houston, 2 May 1972.  The page          
gives the loading sequence, the total penetration in centimeters, and         
the total load in kilograms and Newtons for eight runs of the LSRP.           
There is also a note of a "special point" which is referenced on              
A16_SMSS_72_M016936_036, page C-3 and is the "maverick point" on the          
plot A16_SMSS_72_M016936_034, page C-1.                                       
